tion":{"commit_sha":"b5c6de372064791ff6733ebb9546ec46a1ed2e6f","position":"1785448309428870001-9070aa8c-b2ba-4596-b308-77641d6759b8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f104e44ef54ec50663420d6f54f8b1da0699988a70571e3e2b3d8688937bd86a","event_uuid":"6f365e79-43f0-46b6-bc18-c8dac3d60dd8","position":{"commit_sha":"87fa117800c3a8e2f785b2e14a147795b6566dcf","position":"1785450652109668001-6f365e79-43f0-46b6-bc18-c8dac3d60dd8"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"87817b352bfcd6b0df74137dc38939ab515c0f9aac4c3398d08cfb0e9e68be5d","event_uuid":"58c3bc1a-2298-4ed3-87fc-6023de753cf2","position":{"commit_sha":"87fa117800c3a8e2f785b2e14a147795b6566dcf","position":"1785450652765943001-58c3bc1a-2298-4ed3-87fc-6023de753cf2"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"b94d04901cbb15b705348594084d776b4fddb81106f05a9fe10c711443f680a2","event_uuid":"e22b5942-d169-4563-92dd-d5a27e1fbb9e","position":{"commit_sha":"3f579f286617bec9d09667daa2a95f8d6782d937","position":"1785451134321958136-e22b5942-d169-4563-92dd-d5a27e1fbb9e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"b707f729-f629-4867-9965-f2ea0e303433","comments":[],"created_at":1785447789159405001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"213d722c-dd41-488f-845d-2310eedba814","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ad63-17ad-d545-45d4"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nA single Gerrit Verified run needs 21 concurrent job slots against a GitHub Free org-wide cap of 20 total / 5 macOS, shared with every other navapbc repo. `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` contributes 8 of those, and one of them does no unique work.\n\nThe `import-linter` job installs `-e .[dev]` — byte-identical to `_build-and-test.yml:230` — and runs `pytest tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py tests/unit/test_optional.py`. Those files carry NO pytest markers, and tests/conftest.py only auto-marks `external` under `tests/external/`, so all 9 tests already run in all four `test` matrix cells (3.11/3.12/3.13 + macOS) — strictly more coverage than this job single ubuntu/3.12 run.\n\nThe \"import-leak test defeated by a polluted worker process\" concern does NOT apply here, which is why the deletion is safe: `test_lean_workflow_runtime_pulls_no_heavy_stack` reads `sys.modules` inside a FRESHLY SPAWNED `subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-c\", code])`; `test_no_core_module_imports_heavy_stack_at_module_scope` is a pure `ast.parse` walk over source; and `test_blocked_extra_degrades_friendly` uses the `block_extra` fixture, which EVICTS modules from `sys.modules` and is therefore STRONGER in a loaded worker, not weaker. There is no `COVERAGE_PROCESS_START`/`sitecustomize` in the repo, so even the coverage lane child is a bare interpreter.\n\n## Approach\nDelete the job — and repay, in the same change, the guard it was incidentally providing.\n\nTHE GAP THIS OPENS: nothing in the repo can see the deletion. `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py:131-162` asserts only caller-level WIRING strings (that gerrit-verify invokes the reusable, passes the refspec, that `vote.needs` contains `optionality`). `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py:44-51` reads only caller job keys. NEITHER has any visibility into `_optionality.yml` inner jobs, so both pass unchanged after the deletion.\n\nThat means once the dedicated job is gone, the ONLY thing keeping those 9 tests running is the incidental fact that the two files carry no marker. A future contributor who adds `@pytest.mark.integration`, moves the files, or adds a `paths:` filter deletes the optionality guard with a fully GREEN build. Given this project already has a history of an optionality gap letting bugs reach main, shipping the deletion without a replacement guard is not acceptable.\n\nSo the deletion is paired with a durable, checked-in test asserting those two files are still collected by the default suite selection.\n\nRejected alternative: keep the job. It costs a slot against a cap the run already exceeds, for coverage the matrix strictly dominates.\nRejected alternative: delete without the guard. That converts an explicit check into an implicit one with no alarm.\n\n## Scope\n- `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml` — remove the `import-linter` job only. No other job is touched.\n- `tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` — add the collection guard.\n\nNOT in scope: the per-extra/union collapse (separate ticket ad63-17ad-d545-45d4), `clean-core-wheel`, `_build-and-test.yml`.\n\n## Testing\nThe guard must be durable rather than a one-time check, because the risk is a future edit, not this change.\n\nAdd a test that runs pytest collection over the two files with the default suite selection (`-m \"not integration and not external\"`) and asserts 9 items are collected. Collecting by running the real selection — rather than grepping for marker text — is what makes it catch a marker added anywhere: file-level `pytestmark`, a decorator, or a conftest-applied mark.\n\nThe only real loss from the deletion is diagnostic latency: a heavy-import regression currently reddens a ~1 min job and afterwards surfaces inside a ~15 min matrix cell. That is accepted and recorded here deliberately.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The `import-linter` job no longer exists in `.github/workflows/_optionality.yml`.\n- [ ] No other job in that file is modified.\n- [ ] A checked-in test asserts `tests/unit/test_core_optionality.py` and `tests/unit/test_optional.py` collect 9 items under `-m \"not integration and not external\"`.\n- [ ] That test FAILS if a marker excluding either file from the default selection is added.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py` passes.\n- [ ] `python -m pytest tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py` passes.\n- [ ] `make lint` passes (actionlint covers all workflows).","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":".github/workflows/_optionality.yml","reason":"remove the redundant import-linter job"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_ci_workflow_parity.py","reason":"durable collection guard repaying the deleted job"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","ad63-17ad-d545-45d4"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6f365e79-43f0-46b6-bc18-c8dac3d60dd8","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2132-e48f-425c-4f24","ticket_type":"task","title":"Delete the redundant import-linter job and repay its guard with a collection test","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["52065319-affc-4737-8b51-3606e47b6d78","e39c6456-46b1-4a48-ab77-63c97fa49d96","213d722c-dd41-488f-845d-2310eedba814","4a364c0f-ed6a-4c99-972e-e9748895acf5","9070aa8c-b2ba-4596-b308-77641d6759b8","6f365e79-43f0-46b6-bc18-c8dac3d60dd8","58c3bc1a-2298-4ed3-87fc-6023de753cf2","e22b5942-d169-4563-92dd-d5a27e1fbb9e"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785451134321958137,"uuid":"c1152395-d709-4347-ab0e-b091309d7d96"}